# SILENCE DESIGNS — PREMIUM DISCORD BOT

## Project Overview

I am building a premium Discord bot for **Silence Designs**, a professional ER:LC (Emergency Response: Liberty County) livery and design team.

I want this bot to have the same professional quality as established, feature-rich Discord bots such as Egglord, with a clean architecture, organized source code, professional embeds, persistent interactions, and fully working slash commands.

**CRITICAL: THIS IS A DISCORD BOT PROJECT ONLY. NO WEBSITE AT ALL.**

Do not create a website, landing page, dashboard, web application, browser interface, React frontend, Vite frontend, Next.js application, or website preview.

The final deliverable must be an actual downloadable Discord bot project that I can run locally on my Windows computer and host using my own files.

All customer-facing features must operate inside Discord using slash commands, embeds, buttons, dropdown menus, modals, attachments, and private ticket channels.

I will add custom PNG images for commands, banners, footers, thumbnails, and embeds later. Prepare the project with organized asset folders and configuration references so I can easily add these images without changing the entire codebase.

Do not build a website for managing the bot. Configuration and management must be handled through Discord commands and local configuration files.

## 1. Technology Stack

Use the following technologies:

- Node.js with JavaScript.
- discord.js v14 or a compatible current stable version.
- Discord application slash commands.
- Discord embeds, buttons, select menus, modals, and attachments.
- SQLite for persistent local storage.
- Environment variables using dotenv.
- Modular command and event handlers.
- Proper validation, error handling, permission checks, logging, and restart recovery.
- Google Gemini API for optional AI features.
- A configurable Roblox integration using official or otherwise reliable accessible data sources.

Do not require a paid hosting service to develop or run the bot locally.

Do not put API keys, bot tokens, database credentials, or secrets inside public source code.

The AI features must still allow the bot to start if no Gemini API key is configured.

